{
  "comment": "What a selection inside a piece of prose copies (D-303). The window draws each piece of text (plain text, inline code, code inside a list) as one leaf; leaves are counted from 0 in the order they are drawn. A selection runs from a place to a place, each a leaf and a character in it. Inside one paragraph, heading or block of code only the selected text is copied, with the marks around it. A selection over several of them copies whole lines with their marks: #, -, 1., >, the fence.",
